{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044662-what-is-navigating-the-shadow-like","id":1044662,"title":"What is navigating the Shadow like??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-06T12:30:36-08:00","id":1044662,"title":"What is navigating the Shadow like??","content":"I might be missing something obvious, but I don't feel like I have ever gotten a good grip on what a mage actually see's and feels once he enters the Shadow? Is it just a parallel of the Fallen World, but more Shadowy, or something else entirely? How can I as the ST make a trip into the Shadow interesting and evocative? What themes and aspects of the place should I be trying to get across???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T12:40:11-08:00","id":1044670,"title":"","content":"It's more thoroughly detailed in Werewolf and the Book of Spirits. Everything in it is alive and predatory, but much of it is dormant.<br /> <br /> It's called the Hisil in the First Tongue, spoken by werewolves and spirits, and searching for that might get you better results on the forum. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/976443-hisil\">This thread</a> is pretty good at describing it, or linking to descriptions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/794977-spirit-rite-the-pain-angel\">Here's a hospital.</a><br /> <br /> Long story short, it's dangerous, more than slightly off, and full of living reflections of the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-06-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T13:38:08-08:00","id":1044696,"title":"","content":"yea it's almost if the writers take for granted that you have a working knowledge of OWoDs Umbra cosmology, or have bought the book of spirits, or have picked apart first edition Forsaken (not the core book mind you but the whole of the series.)<br /> <br /> you can use it as you see fit it is the &quot;Other World&quot;; a dark monster filled reflection within a dark monster filled reflection.<br /> <br /> A couple thing I keep in mind when including it.<br /> Always keep events happening in the shadow relevant to the material plane. This is really important it keeps the shadow realm form being a Fantasy world that characters travel to, that has it's place but not normally the Shadow. Spirits create cults, thralls, hosts and people worship, study, and merge with Spirits. and of course spirits themselves alter the emotions and situations of those living near them. <br /> The Shadow Realm is not a spot to hang out keep it strange, alien, dangerous. If the characters think that the shadow would be the perfect base or hide out or hiding spot, dissuade them. Awake Spirits are sapient living concepts. They have there own language, desires, machinations, and society. Spirit culture is often described as feudal although this makes sense and is technically accurate with how the life cycle of Spirits and essence work mechanically it is not thoroughly descriptive and even a little misleading. the more of your game that involves Spirits the more you should detail you should give their society. but it naturally plays with themes of appeasement, consumption, cannibalism and purity. <br /> There are no generic spirits Every Spirit is a Spirit of something real, a real fire, a real building, real suffering, real fear, real abuse, real hope, real love. <br /> <br /> examples sources:<br /> the Upside Down form Stranger Things<br /> Wonderland form Alice in Wonderland<br /> Silent Hill<br /> XXX Holic; mostly inferred from mortal and &quot;mage&quot; perspective. <br /> Lord of the Rings; whenever Frodo wears the ring he enters twilight, i've never seen it any other way. <br /> Avatar: the Last Airbender/Legend of Korra; the both lightly explore a spirit world it's a good starting point from my perspective, if rather kid friendly for the world of darkness. but the mist that makes you forget, and the face stealing centipede are perfect. <br /> Spirited away; it's a classic, watch it. pay attention to the interactions between the Spirits very good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T13:52:58-08:00","id":1044707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar252_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"252\" data-vbnamecard=\"252\">basketcase</a> It's more like they've got limited word count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T09:33:14-08:00","id":1045155,"title":"","content":"Reposting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar375_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"375\" data-vbnamecard=\"375\">Papa Bear</a> s description cause its just so good:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does the Shadow look like?<br /> <br /> You\u2019ll have to go on a bit of a trip with me to get a picture of what I see when I imagine the Shadow Realm.<br /> <br /> Have you ever done a drawing with markers on a pad of paper and pressed so hard or run over the same space on the paper so many times that it bleeds thru to the pages underneath? If not, go try it, because the rest of this won\u2019t make much sense.<br /> <br /> Imagine if an artist was to draw a picture of a factory with the cityscape behind it every day with marker. Every day, he draws the same picture from memory, but he\u2019s not allowed to look at yesterday\u2019s picture for reference. It has to be from memory every single time. The places that are important to him will get the most detail and greatest attention. Places that are less important will be drawn with ever decreasing attention. Because the places that are important will be drawn more heavily, they will bleed thru to the next page, making it easier to remember them. Places less important will fade over time until forgotten all together. New things may be added to the picture, even over a place that was once occupied by a forgotten object. Now imagine that not just one artist got to draw that factory and cityscape, but <i>everybody</i> who works at that place on that day got to draw it, but they are all on the same piece of paper and with the same markers. Places like the factory that employs half the town would be drawn so heavily that it goes thru several days\u2019 worth of paper, except for the individual variations. The window washer who works there will know every broken window, but the foreman won\u2019t. Other places that are important to only a few people will not fade as quickly, but the old factory that only a derelict hides out in will not be all that noticeable compared to the thousands of lines of the factory.<br /> <br /> Still with me? From here, we imagine that the images drawn are done by more Expressionist and/or Impressionist artists, i.e. it is a little more subjective than Realism and they\u2019re trying to convey the feelings people have about it. While most of the objects retain their primary shapes, the drill press is not just a drill press\u2026.it has chains around the bottom because the one guy gets stuck working on it for a month. It\u2019s also got a drill 3 times too big because of the 50 guys who are missing fingers because they go too close. The cars in the parking lot shuffle around slightly like herd animals, but generally stay in one spot. The mini-vans and SUVs look more like covered wagons designed by Chrysler, metal and plastic, but clearly built for hauling stuff and people over long distances. The executives fancy cars move more like sleek gazelles, except for the president\u2019s Mustang which is, of course, a horse with a large penis (no, really, he\u2019s not compensating for anything!). The factory itself looks both beneficial and ominous. The lights inside look more like hellfires, the smoke stacks produce a dark green smoke, but there are also dollar signs coming out of it pointing in the direction of many of the houses.<br /> <br /> The last element to be added is that all the markers used are mixed with charcoal and ash. They\u2019re dark and rough (charcoal) or washed out and gritty (ash). The factory isn\u2019t a good, healthy work environment, so it looks worse than a lot of other places. Lots of injuries and deaths, but people work there because they are short on options. The city behind it is a little brighter because those are the places people go to escape the work: home, bars, clubs, shopping, etc. Those places that have become less distinct are shrouded in a haze or over-shadowed by the other places that stand out.<br /> <br /> Above it all shines Mother Luna, there is no direct sunlight here. It is dusk or full night, depending on how bright Luna shines that day. The shadows are long and things hide in them. </div> </div> </div>This is originally found in the discussion that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> linked above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:43:03-08:00","id":1045314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1044662-what-is-navigating-the-shadow-like?p=1045155#post1045155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reposting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar375_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"375\" data-vbnamecard=\"375\">Papa Bear</a> s description cause its just so good:</div> </div> </div> </div>I must've had a very good day when I wrote that. It's been linked/quoted/reposted enough times I might qualify as a meme now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T09:09:43-08:00","id":1045808,"title":"","content":"These are all great responses, thanks very much everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T20:48:08-08:00","id":1046160,"title":"","content":"I always thought Silent Hill pretty much nails it. Papa Bear's description pretty much describes Silent Hill without the added fact that both the Hisil and Silent Hill are completely dog eat dog. Eat or be eaten literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 02-08-2017, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T12:04:17-08:00","id":1046405,"title":"","content":"Yeah, for dealing with things in the Shadow, I had to put another post:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's my best advice on running things in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> 1) Don't worry about the <i>actual </i>terrain as much as the <i>impressionist </i>terrain. Does the area <b>look </b>rocky and dangerous in the material realm? Then it probably is. Does it <b>look </b>like it might be filled with tranquil lakes and easy trails in the material realm? Then it probably is. The Shadow is a reflection of the <i>impressions </i>and <i>feelings </i>of the area. If no one is sure what's up there, then it might look more foreboding with dark areas due to the extreme tree cover, which also makes it a little claustrophobic.<br /> <br /> 2) I usually treat the interactions with the spirits in the Shadow like an amusement park horror house, but instead of people in masks wandering around, they let loose a bunch of wild animals. The characters will wander thru stretches of general shadowy areas, then suddenly something will jump out at them, and it'll either disappear just as suddenly or go straight for the characters. The weaker (prey) spirits will jump thru and scamper back off into the darkness. The stronger (predator) spirits will see potential prey in the characters and go after them. A quick, ferocious, and bloody battle takes place and then the whole place gets quiet again. Too quiet. Like everybody's watching now.<br /> <br /> 3) Not every spirit is <b>awake</b>. The majority of the spirits are just filling in the exact space that their material counterpart has. The tree spirits are there for the trees. The rock spirits are there as rocks. The wild sheep and rams spirits are just grazing on the grass spirits and the grass isn't trying to move away from them. Most of them are barely beyond motes. The dangerous ones are the ones who have started to stray from their material anchors. These are the ones who've been snacking on other spirits that may or may not be an acceptable part of it's diet. The owl spirit who's been dining on mice and rabbits is fine. The owl spirit feeding on darkness and flight spirits is just getting more specialized, but still not far off from where it started. The owl spirit who's been scooping up <i>wolf </i>spirits and <i>tree</i> spirits.......<i><b>that thing ain't right!!</b></i><br /> <br /> 4) While spirits are generally hostile to the Uratha, not all of them will outright <i>attack </i>them. Some of them are small enough and weak enough to know they don't stand a chance. So they run and they hide and they <b><i><u>WATCH</u></i></b><u><i><b>!</b></i></u> Oh my goodness, the number of eyes staring out from the darkness in the Shadow is enough to make even the most level-headed turn paranoid. And what are they watching for? An opportunity. Maybe the characters know a way out to the material realm. Maybe something bigger will come along and rough them up enough to make them easy picking. Maybe something will just tear them apart and the others can take the scraps. While not every spirit will <i>attack</i>, they are still willing to become a <i>predator</i> (or scavenger) if the prey is weak enough. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:20:46-08:00","id":1046899,"title":"","content":"Whenever this topic comes up, I always sing the praises of Mr. Shopping's actual play, Detroit Rock City.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar\"> Four Werewolves walk into a bar. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/860086-four-werewolves-walk-into-a-bar </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Title unrelated. So I'm going to be running Werewolf 2nd ed since my group wanted to play something other than Demon; I've been running the Descent since it came out. Anyways. All those years games of Demon and I'm not really sure how to do Werewolf? I understand the core concept of the game I've read the Core for both 1st and 2nd edition. But clearly Werewolf is nothing like Demon. So a few things. Is it Closer to Monster of the Week or can a hunt take chapters worth of doing and then final out with &amp;quot;The Big hunt&amp;quot; Since werewolves have to protect their territory, It's not so easy as a </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200b<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462775-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-werewolf-2e-edition?p=839392#post839392\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...392#post839392</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}